    "body": "This PR cleans up three tests that still carry code or text from the legacy wallet:\n\n- `wallet_address_types.py`: the send loop iterates over `do_multisigs = [False]`, so its multisig code path and the multisig cases of `test_address`/`test_desc` can't run. That code path is also broken, since it never sets the address it checks. This PR removes that code, along with the docstring section about the old `addmultisigaddress` tests.\n\n- `wallet_backup.py`: the docstring still describes `dumpwallet`/`importwallet` and erasing wallets; the test uses `backupwallet` and `restorewallet`.\n\n- `wallet_hd.py`: `-keypool=0` does nothing for descriptor wallets, which always keep at least one key, and the test config already sets `keypool=1`.\n\nNo coverage changes: `wallet_address_types.py` runs the same 8 send iterations before and after.",
